From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 21 Aug 2026 22:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] power: reset: msm-poweroff: deassert PS_HOLD through the secure world

On some Qualcomm SoCs the PS_HOLD register is not writable from the non-secure
world: the store is accepted and discarded, and the platform stays up. msm8998
is one of them. Its downstream kernel calls into TZ instead, and only falls
back to the register write "in case the scm_call returns".

Do the same. Query once at probe whether the firmware implements the call, and
use it in front of the existing write. Where the call is absent - which is
every SoC mainline supports today - nothing changes.

This patch alone has no visible effect on a platform whose firmware also
provides PSCI, because the PSCI restart handler is registered at priority 129
and outranks this driver's 128. Raising the priority is a separate change, and
deliberately comes later in this series.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
--- a/drivers/power/reset/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/Kconfig
@@ -140,6 +140,7 @@
 config POWER_RESET_MSM
 	bool "Qualcomm MSM power-off driver"
 	depends on ARCH_QCOM
+	depends on QCOM_SCM
 	help
 	  Power off and restart support for Qualcomm boards.
 
--- a/drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c
@@ -13,10 +13,26 @@
 #include <linux/reboot.h>
 #include <linux/pm.h>
 
+#include <linux/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h>
+
 static void __iomem *msm_ps_hold;
 
+/*
+ * On some SoCs -- msm8998 is the one this was found on -- PS_HOLD is owned by
+ * the secure world and the bare register write below is silently ignored, so
+ * the platform never goes down. The vendor driver drops it with an SCM call
+ * and keeps the write only as a fallback "in case the scm_call returns".
+ *
+ * Cached at probe because the availability query issues a sleeping SCM call
+ * and the restart path runs with interrupts off.
+ */
+static bool scm_owns_ps_hold;
+
 static int do_msm_poweroff(struct sys_off_data *data)
 {
+	if (scm_owns_ps_hold)
+		qcom_scm_deassert_ps_hold();
+
 	writel(0, msm_ps_hold);
 	mdelay(10000);
 
@@ -29,6 +45,10 @@
 	if (IS_ERR(msm_ps_hold))
 		return PTR_ERR(msm_ps_hold);
 
+	scm_owns_ps_hold = qcom_scm_deassert_ps_hold_available();
+	dev_info(&pdev->dev, "PS_HOLD deassert: %s\n",
+		 scm_owns_ps_hold ? "secure world" : "register write only");
+
 	devm_register_sys_off_handler(&pdev->dev, SYS_OFF_MODE_RESTART,
 				      128, do_msm_poweroff, NULL);
 
-- 
